ring texts in dict T.\n\nThen print regex windows for \"Self Consistency\", \"Tree of Thoughts\", \"CAMEL\", \"Generative Agents\", \"evaluat\".\n\nLog truncation will cut output; so print limited amount per pattern. Use w=250.\n\nActually the paper: Section 2.1 reasoning techniques. Self-consistency: majority vote over reasoning paths. Tree of Thoughts: two search controllers? Likely \"a simple BFS or DFS search\" ... Actually ToT paper describes search via BFS/DFS with a state evaluator. The survey may say \"Two search controllers: breadth-first and depth-first search\". So tot_search = [\"breadth_first\", \"depth_first\"] or \"depth_first_search\"/\"breadth_first_search\".\n\nCAMEL: \"role-playing\" with \"inception prompting\"? CAMEL uses \"role-playing\" with \"task-specifier\" and \"inception prompt\". The survey may say \"CAMEL uses role-playing with inception prompting\". Field camel_prompting lowercase underscore.\n\nGenerative Agents evaluators: 1000 human evaluators? The Generative Agents paper used 100 human evaluators... Actually the \"Generative Agents\" paper had a believability evaluation with 100 human evaluators rating. I recall \"100 human evaluators\". Need to verify from text.\n\nLet's do it."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8815,"completion_tokens":739,"total_tokens":9554,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4352},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":501},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4352,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":4463},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}